he act or opportunity of choosing or the thing chosen.\nL73: \nL74: 【20†choice】 suggests the opportunity or privilege of choosing freely.\nL75: \nL76: freedom of choice\nL77: 【24†option】 implies a power to choose that is specifically granted or guaranteed.\nL78: \nL79: the option of paying now or later\nL80: \nL81: 【25†alternative】 implies a need to choose one and reject another possibility.\nL82: \nL83: equally attractive alternatives\nL84: \nL85: 【26†preference】 suggests a choice guided by one's judgment or predilections.\nL86: \nL87: a preference for cool weather\nL88: \nL89: 【23†selection】 implies a range of choice.\nL90: \nL91: a varied selection of furniture\nL92: \nL93: 【27†election】 implies an end or purpose which requires exercise of judgment.\nL94: doing a tax return forces certain elections on you\nL95: ## Examples of election in a Sentence\nL96: \nL97: He's favored to win the election. The scandal may affect his chances for election. Her election to the Senate was a surprise to many.\nL98: \nL99: Recent Examples on the Web\nL100: \nL101: Examples are automatically compiled from online sources to show current usage. 【14†Read More】 Opinions expressed in the examples do not represent those of Merriam-Webster or its editors. 【28†Send us feedback†docs.google.com】.\nL102: The chaos was a fitting end to one of the ugliest elections in recent years, said Paulo César de Oliveira in Correio da Manhã (Rio de Janeiro). — The Week Uk, TheWeek, 31 Oct. 2026 California voters face a crowded November ballot packed with questions on taxes, special elections and environmental rules. — Stephen Hobbs, Sacbee.com, 31 Oct. 2026 Historic amounts of money have flowed into this year's midterm elections. — Arkansas Online, 31 Oct.\nL103: 2026 Bolsonaro, who is under investigation in Brazil over allegations of corruption and money laundering, refused to concede and has called the elections fraudulent, without providing evidence. — Eléonore Hughes, Los Angeles Times, 31 Oct. 2026 【29†See All Example Sentences for election】\nL104: ## Word History\nL105: \nL106: First Known Use\nL107: \nL108: 13th century, in the meaning defined at 【30†sense 1a】\nL109: \nL110: Time Traveler\nL111: \nL112: The first known use of election was in the 13th century\nL113: \nL114: 【31†See more words from the same century】\nL115: \nL116: ## Browse Nearby Words\nL117: \nL118: 【32†electable】\nL119: \nL120: election\nL121: \nL122: 【33†election cake】\nL123: \nL124: 【34†See all Nearby Words】\nL125: ## Articles Related to election\nL126: \nL127: 【35†A Briefing on the 'College' in... The Electoral College vs The College of Registered Voters】 【36†'Nail-Biter', 'Battleground State', and... The history behind 9 words from the news】 【37†What's a 'downticket candidate'? And what's a 'downballot race'?】\nL128: \nL129: ## Cite this Entry\nL130: \nL131: Style\nL132: \nL133: [Select]\nL134: \nL135: “Election.” Merriam-Webster.com Dictionary, Merriam-Webster, https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/election. Accessed 1 Nov. 2026.\nL136: \nL137: 【38†Image†prod.cdn-mw.com】Copy Citation\nL138: ## Kids Definition\nL139: \nL140: election\nL141: \nL142: noun\nL143: \nL144: elec·​tion 【16†i-ˈlek-shən 】\nL145: \nL146: 1\nL147: \nL148: : an act or process of electing\nL149: \nL150: especially : the process of voting to choose a person for office\nL151: \nL152: the election of a new governor\nL153: \nL154: 2\nL155: \nL156: : the fact of being elected\nL157: \nL158: her election to the presidency\nL159: ## Legal Definition\nL160: \nL161: election\nL162: \nL163: noun\nL164: \nL165: elec·​tion\nL166: \nL167: 1\nL168: \nL169: a\nL170: \nL171: : the act or process of electing\nL172: \nL173: b\nL174: \nL175: : an instance of the electorate voting for candidates for an elective office\nL176: \nL177: c\nL178: \nL179: : the fact of being elected\nL180: \nL181: 2\nL182: \nL183: : the right, power, or privilege of making a choice: as\nL184: \nL185: a\nL186: \nL187: : the right of a spouse to choose a statutorily prescribed amount of a deceased spouse's estate or whatever was devised to him or her under the will\nL188: \nL189: b\nL190: : the right of a person who has an interest in property that a deceased has disposed of by will either to claim his or her right to the property or to accept what he or she was devised under the will instead\nL191: \nL192: c\nL193: \nL194: : the right of a party to a contract that has been breached by the other party to choose to continue or terminate the contract see also 【39†election of remedies】, 【40†equitable election】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReferendum - UK Parliament (https://www.parliament.uk/site-information/glossary/referendum/)\nciteturn24view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.parliament.uk/site-information/glossary/referendum/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 228\nL0: 【0††www.googletagmanager.com】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Skip to main content】 【2†Menu】\nL3: \nL4: Menu\nL5: \nL6: Select an area to explore\nL7: \nL8:   * 【2†Business】\nL9:   * 【2†MPs, Lords & offices】\nL10:   * 【2†About】\nL11:   * 【2†Get involved】\nL12:   * 【2†Visit】\nL13:   * 【2†Learning】\nL14:   * 【3†Shop†www.shop.parliament.uk】\nL15:   * 【2†More】\nL16: \nL17:   * Or type a keyword to search\nL18: \nL19: [Input: Search UK Parliament]\nL20: \nL21: [Button: Search]\nL22: \nL23: 【2†Close】\nL24: \nL25: [Input]\nL26: \nL27: 【2†Close】\nL28: ## Parliamentary business\nL29: \nL30: Find out what’s on today at the House of Commons and House of Lords. Track current bills, keep up with committees, watch live footage and follow topical issues.\nL31: \nL32: 【2†Close】 【2†Back】 【2†Close】\nL33: ### In this section\nL34: \nL35:   * 【4†Parliamentary business home】\nL36:   * 【5†House of Commons】\nL37:   * 【6†House of Lords】\nL38:   * 【7†What's on†calendar.parliament.uk】\nL39:   * 【8†Bills & legislation】\nL40:   * 【9†Committees†committees.parliament.uk】\nL41:   * 【